    "updated_at": "2026-11-04T16:44:43Z",
    "body": "All three engines ([Blink](https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/blink/renderer/core/html/parser/html_construction_site.cc;l=248-278;drc=7a5e9d918c398f8838f1b8c5fc7b5b49f71a6065), [WebKit](https://github.com/WebKit/WebKit/blob/a5f7510f0d6fb16a72b0f1b976fc5f9793a89a4d/Source/WebCore/html/parser/HTMLConstructionSite.cpp#L763-L777), [Gecko](https://searchfox.org/mozilla-central/rev/752bef935dc1b9ef5cfca9bd6bb3cd6e16ab5cb5/parser/html/nsHtml5TreeOperation.cpp#254-339)) coalesce contiguous character tokens and, when appending a flushed run to an existing `Text` node, behave like DOM's [replace data](https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-cd-replace): running the parent's [children changed steps](https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-node-children-changed-ext) and queueing a `\"characterData\"` `MutationRecord`.\n\nWhat if we standardized the existing pending-text/flush-pending-text mechanism that's shared across the engines (% quirks like WebKit's 64k max buffer size)?\n",
